1
00:00:01,067 --> 00:00:01,933
<i>Boss, I already saw the people
looking for you.</i>

2
00:00:02,067 --> 00:00:03,467
<i>I'm covering the raid as media.</i>

3
00:00:03,600 --> 00:00:05,500
<i>But since it's official
and government-sanctioned,</i>

4
00:00:05,633 --> 00:00:06,500
<i> civilians are not allowed.</i>

5
00:00:06,633 --> 00:00:08,233
<i> You cannot join the operation.</i>

6
00:00:08,367 --> 00:00:11,633
<i>Your brother-in-law will bring
nothing good to this mission.</i>

7
00:00:11,767 --> 00:00:12,867
<i> Does he know about you?</i>

8
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:15,267
<i>If he knows,
he won't expose himself.</i>

9
00:00:15,400 --> 00:00:16,300
<i>So it looks like
he still doesn't know yet.</i>

10
00:00:16,433 --> 00:00:18,767
<i>You should leave
before Andrew sees you.</i>

11
00:00:18,900 --> 00:00:19,800
<i> Stop here, Sir.</i>

12
00:00:19,933 --> 00:00:22,067
<i>Sorry, I don't need
the ride anymore.</i>

13
00:00:22,200 --> 00:00:23,300
<i> You just wasted my time.</i>

14
00:00:23,433 --> 00:00:26,700
<i>150,000 Lumen-X pills
are on their way</i>

15
00:00:26,833 --> 00:00:28,500
<i> to Valmora as we speak.</i>

16
00:00:28,633 --> 00:00:29,567
<i> The item?</i>

17
00:00:29,700 --> 00:00:31,233
<i>It's all set, Boss.
Ready for dispatch.</i>

18
00:00:31,367 --> 00:00:34,033
<i>This is a major operation.
The meetup is high value.</i>

19
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:35,933
<i>Boss, we're here. Have you left?</i>

20
00:00:36,067 --> 00:00:37,600
<i>No, I'm staying.
Let's finish this.</i>

21
00:00:37,733 --> 00:00:41,300
<i>Target site is the
Sanctuary at Valmora.</i>

22
00:00:41,433 --> 00:00:44,667
<i>We're working with the theory
that their deal is with Berdugo.</i>

23
00:00:44,800 --> 00:00:47,100
<i>Dad needs to know
about the transaction.</i>

24
00:00:47,233 --> 00:00:48,400
<i> Where are you, Berdugo?</i>

25
00:00:48,533 --> 00:00:51,033
<i>Orders from Ma'am Delilah
for the guest.</i>

26
00:00:51,167 --> 00:00:51,933
<i> Bring it in.</i>

27
00:00:52,067 --> 00:00:53,333
<i> Let's seal the deal then.</i>

28
00:00:53,467 --> 00:00:55,333
<i> Cheers to new partnerships.</i>

29
00:00:55,467 --> 00:00:56,267
<i>To partnership.
[CLINKS]</i>

30
00:00:56,400 --> 00:00:57,633
<i> Shall we start then?</i>

31
00:00:57,767 --> 00:01:00,567
<i>Andrew is surely still here.
It's risky, he might catch you.</i>

32
00:01:00,700 --> 00:01:03,833
<i>I would prefer you hurry
and start the transaction.</i>

33
00:01:03,967 --> 00:01:06,167
<i>You're in such a hurry.
Why is that?</i>

34
00:01:06,300 --> 00:01:09,200
<i>Could it be those people
chasing you?</i>

35
00:01:09,367 --> 00:01:10,867
<i>They're just small fry
competition.</i>

36
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:13,200
<i>It needs to be safe,
so you don't have to worry it.</i>

37
00:01:13,333 --> 00:01:17,633
<i>I already told my men to chase
them down and eliminate them.</i>

38
00:01:35,767 --> 00:01:40,133
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

39
00:01:42,800 --> 00:01:47,667
- [GRUNTING]
- [THUDDING]

40
00:01:50,333 --> 00:01:52,533
Come on, Team. Let's move!

41
00:01:52,667 --> 00:01:55,633
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

42
00:02:06,533 --> 00:02:08,567
Bravo, secure exit.

43
00:02:10,967 --> 00:02:13,200
Alpha, follow me.
Ramos, take the lead.

44
00:02:16,767 --> 00:02:18,600
You too, Andrew, follow me.

45
00:02:26,533 --> 00:02:29,967
The transaction will happen
at Berdugo's villa.

46
00:02:30,100 --> 00:02:33,033
Wait, you'll face
two big syndicates.

47
00:02:33,167 --> 00:02:34,400
And only four of you
will storm in?

48
00:02:34,533 --> 00:02:38,267
It's a quick handoff,
but we still planned it.

49
00:02:38,400 --> 00:02:39,767
The others are nearby,
spread out.

50
00:02:39,900 --> 00:02:40,867
There, look.

51
00:02:42,233 --> 00:02:44,967
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

52
00:02:47,267 --> 00:02:49,800
Who gave you the right
to interfere in my affairs?

53
00:02:49,933 --> 00:02:54,433
My dear, I was under the
impression that we were a team.

54
00:02:54,567 --> 00:02:57,167
No, Delilah. We are not allies.

55
00:02:57,300 --> 00:02:59,933
We are just businessmen
closing a deal.

56
00:03:00,067 --> 00:03:01,267
That's all.

57
00:03:01,400 --> 00:03:03,900
So now, let's begin
the transaction.

58
00:03:04,033 --> 00:03:05,267
Very well.

59
00:03:07,100 --> 00:03:09,633
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

60
00:03:36,533 --> 00:03:38,733
Madam, this is ready.

61
00:03:38,867 --> 00:03:40,033
Good.

62
00:03:52,600 --> 00:03:53,600
[CLACKS]

63
00:03:53,733 --> 00:03:54,700
What was that?

64
00:03:54,867 --> 00:03:58,300
[FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]

65
00:04:00,233 --> 00:04:01,400
Don't worry.

66
00:04:01,533 --> 00:04:02,867
You're protected.

67
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:04,533
Protected?
I don't need protection.

68
00:04:04,667 --> 00:04:05,900
Hey!

69
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:09,167
What are you doing?

70
00:04:09,300 --> 00:04:10,000
Wait.

71
00:04:10,133 --> 00:04:11,433
Why do you look like that?

72
00:04:11,567 --> 00:04:14,433
- [THUDDING]
- [GRUNTING]

73
00:04:19,567 --> 00:04:22,900
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

74
00:04:30,967 --> 00:04:32,667
You really just watched me,
didn't you?

75
00:04:32,800 --> 00:04:34,833
We can't make noise.

76
00:04:34,967 --> 00:04:35,933
Hey!

77
00:04:36,067 --> 00:04:37,400
[GUN FIRES]

78
00:04:38,667 --> 00:04:39,833
[GASPS]

79
00:04:39,967 --> 00:04:41,700
- Boss...
- What was that?

80
00:04:41,833 --> 00:04:44,533
Could it be those people
looking for you?

81
00:04:44,667 --> 00:04:46,600
I thought they were small fry?

82
00:04:49,367 --> 00:04:52,300
- [GRUNTING]
- [THUDDING]

83
00:04:56,833 --> 00:04:58,533
Let's move! Come on.

84
00:05:01,433 --> 00:05:03,333
Anjo, secure Madam.
I'll handle this.

85
00:05:03,467 --> 00:05:04,633
- Boss, let's go!
- Go, Madam.

86
00:05:04,767 --> 00:05:07,467
- I'll take care of this, go on.
- Berdugo, this way.

87
00:05:09,033 --> 00:05:12,133
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

88
00:05:12,267 --> 00:05:13,233
[GUN FIRING]

89
00:05:13,367 --> 00:05:15,233
- [GOON SPEAKS INDISTINCTLY]
- This way, Boss.

90
00:05:17,267 --> 00:05:20,100
[GUN FIRING]

91
00:05:20,233 --> 00:05:21,633
They shouldn't get away.

92
00:05:21,767 --> 00:05:25,400
[MULTIPLE SHOTS FIRED]

93
00:05:44,733 --> 00:05:45,833
[TIRES SCREECHING]

94
00:05:45,967 --> 00:05:48,967
- [GUN FIRING IN DISTANCE]
- [MULTIPLE SHOTS FIRED]

95
00:06:38,067 --> 00:06:39,033
Let's go!

96
00:06:39,167 --> 00:06:41,200
There's a group moving
towards the parking area.

97
00:06:41,367 --> 00:06:43,867
It could be Berdugo. Intercept!

98
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:47,367
- [GUN FIRING]
- [TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

99
00:06:56,300 --> 00:06:58,367
[GRUNTS]

100
00:06:58,500 --> 00:07:05,500
[TIRES SCREECHING]

101
00:07:05,633 --> 00:07:06,767
Boss!

102
00:07:07,833 --> 00:07:10,100
Hide, Boss! Castro, let's go!

103
00:07:10,233 --> 00:07:13,200
[GUN FIRING]

104
00:07:19,167 --> 00:07:20,800
[GUN CLICKING]

105
00:07:20,933 --> 00:07:21,467
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

106
00:07:24,567 --> 00:07:26,900
DDE! Open the door!

107
00:07:29,067 --> 00:07:30,333
[CLACKS]

108
00:07:30,467 --> 00:07:32,767
[GUN FIRING]

109
00:07:33,800 --> 00:07:34,933
[GASPS]

110
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:40,533
- [GROANS]
- [GUN FIRING]

111
00:07:46,733 --> 00:07:49,700
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

112
00:07:54,567 --> 00:07:59,500
Zoey, damn you! I trusted you!
I even told you my plans!

113
00:07:59,633 --> 00:08:01,500
You still have time to change,
Francis!

114
00:08:01,633 --> 00:08:02,633
Surrender now!

115
00:08:02,767 --> 00:08:04,233
You're insane!

116
00:08:04,367 --> 00:08:07,300
[GUN FIRING]

117
00:08:07,433 --> 00:08:08,800
You're the ones
who should surrender!

118
00:08:08,933 --> 00:08:10,633
You entered the wrong den!

119
00:08:10,767 --> 00:08:12,700
[GUN FIRING]

120
00:08:19,400 --> 00:08:21,100
[GRUNTS]

121
00:08:22,733 --> 00:08:24,533
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

122
00:08:25,833 --> 00:08:26,967
Joey?

123
00:08:27,100 --> 00:08:32,867
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

124
00:08:41,300 --> 00:08:44,267
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

125
00:08:51,267 --> 00:08:52,833
[THUDS]

126
00:08:54,133 --> 00:08:56,033
What the hell is she doing here?

127
00:08:56,933 --> 00:08:59,367
- [GRUNTING]
- [GROANING]

128
00:08:59,500 --> 00:09:01,300
[THUDDING]

129
00:09:17,067 --> 00:09:19,067
- [THUDS]
- [GROANS]

130
00:09:21,233 --> 00:09:22,767
[GROANING]

131
00:09:25,100 --> 00:09:27,067
[GRUNTING]

132
00:09:30,767 --> 00:09:32,200
[INTENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

133
00:09:36,967 --> 00:09:38,067
[GROANS]

134
00:09:40,067 --> 00:09:41,200
[GUN FIRING]

135
00:09:41,333 --> 00:09:43,733
[INTENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

136
00:09:45,800 --> 00:09:47,867
- [GRUNTING]
- [GROANING]

137
00:10:03,900 --> 00:10:05,367
You poor thing.

138
00:10:05,500 --> 00:10:07,200
No one will help you now.

139
00:10:08,133 --> 00:10:11,400
[INTENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

140
00:10:11,533 --> 00:10:13,100
[PANTING]

141
00:10:13,867 --> 00:10:15,767
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

142
00:10:16,700 --> 00:10:18,367
[THUDS]

143
00:10:28,300 --> 00:10:30,900
Francis Toledo,
you are under arrest!

144
00:10:31,033 --> 00:10:34,000
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

145
00:10:38,633 --> 00:10:40,967
So, Valmora...

146
00:10:41,100 --> 00:10:44,533
If this goes clean,
what happens next?

147
00:10:44,667 --> 00:10:46,367
Pray that it goes well.

148
00:10:46,500 --> 00:10:49,733
And if Berdugo's in a good mood,
then maybe...

149
00:10:49,867 --> 00:10:51,633
maybe he will give you time.

150
00:10:51,767 --> 00:10:53,333
Really?

151
00:10:53,467 --> 00:10:55,467
Maybe is all I get?

152
00:10:55,600 --> 00:10:57,800
That's how his world works.

153
00:10:57,933 --> 00:11:00,233
[PHONE RINGING]

154
00:11:03,900 --> 00:11:04,800
Matias...

155
00:11:04,933 --> 00:11:07,000
The DDE raided the transaction
in Valmora.

156
00:11:07,133 --> 00:11:08,700
<i>The items and money were seized.</i>

157
00:11:08,867 --> 00:11:09,500
What?

158
00:11:09,633 --> 00:11:11,200
Yes, everything's gone.

159
00:11:11,333 --> 00:11:12,900
Boss is wounded.

160
00:11:14,933 --> 00:11:16,433
He says he needs to talk to us.

161
00:11:16,567 --> 00:11:18,133
All right, I'm heading there.

162
00:11:18,267 --> 00:11:19,267
I'm coming with you.

163
00:11:19,400 --> 00:11:20,967
No.

164
00:11:21,100 --> 00:11:23,033
Stay here.

165
00:11:23,167 --> 00:11:25,167
This is not the right time.

166
00:11:31,867 --> 00:11:35,833
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

167
00:11:37,667 --> 00:11:39,333
[EXHALES]

168
00:11:47,500 --> 00:11:49,333
[BIRDS CHIRPING]

169
00:11:55,800 --> 00:11:57,500
We've lost 500 million pesos,

170
00:11:57,633 --> 00:11:59,100
and your brother-in-law
even shot you.

171
00:11:59,233 --> 00:12:01,600
Let's not focus on the losses,
Matias.

172
00:12:01,900 --> 00:12:05,367
We still have fast-moving items
because of strong demand.

173
00:12:05,500 --> 00:12:09,067
Do you think Andrew
recognized you?

174
00:12:09,200 --> 00:12:11,133
He wouldn't just shoot me

175
00:12:11,267 --> 00:12:13,100
if he knew his brother-in-law
was the one he was chasing.

176
00:12:13,233 --> 00:12:15,433
But he still shot you.

177
00:12:16,567 --> 00:12:17,867
What do we do now?

178
00:12:18,000 --> 00:12:19,567
Let him be.

179
00:12:21,033 --> 00:12:22,500
Let him chase Berdugo.

180
00:12:22,633 --> 00:12:24,333
The more he focuses
on that name,

181
00:12:24,467 --> 00:12:26,700
the less he looks at me.

182
00:12:26,833 --> 00:12:28,667
And men like Andrew...

183
00:12:30,667 --> 00:12:34,033
They don't know when to stop,
and that's what will kill him.

184
00:12:34,167 --> 00:12:35,800
[UNEASY MUSIC CONTINUES]

185
00:12:41,500 --> 00:12:42,833
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

186
00:12:42,967 --> 00:12:44,067
Why, Boss?

187
00:12:49,200 --> 00:12:50,500
One of my cufflinks is missing.

188
00:12:50,633 --> 00:12:53,833
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

189
00:13:02,600 --> 00:13:04,333
Hurry up!

190
00:13:04,467 --> 00:13:05,933
Bring those in!

191
00:13:17,900 --> 00:13:19,033
Are you okay?

192
00:13:20,533 --> 00:13:22,433
Thank you for saving me.

193
00:13:23,300 --> 00:13:24,600
I'm just doing my job.

194
00:13:25,567 --> 00:13:26,967
But if you really want
to repay me,

195
00:13:27,100 --> 00:13:29,133
you could give up Andrew.

196
00:13:32,300 --> 00:13:33,900
Of course, sure.

197
00:13:35,000 --> 00:13:37,400
Relax.
[CHUCKLES]

198
00:13:37,533 --> 00:13:39,100
I'm just joking.

199
00:13:40,133 --> 00:13:42,133
But seriously, I didn't know
you were that good

200
00:13:42,267 --> 00:13:43,567
at fighting, Joey.

201
00:13:44,633 --> 00:13:46,700
My father taught me.

202
00:13:48,767 --> 00:13:49,933
About that...

203
00:13:50,067 --> 00:13:53,100
We didn't get Berdugo
like we wanted.

204
00:13:53,767 --> 00:13:56,433
But at least it's clear he's
the one Delilah is dealing with.

205
00:13:56,600 --> 00:13:59,433
Did we get any identification
on him?

206
00:13:59,567 --> 00:14:00,333
None.

207
00:14:01,300 --> 00:14:03,800
I had the entire resort's CCTV
checked,

208
00:14:03,933 --> 00:14:06,433
but it hasn't been operational
for three days.

209
00:14:07,967 --> 00:14:09,933
It was deliberately done
so there'd be no recording.

210
00:14:11,300 --> 00:14:12,433
Exactly.

211
00:14:13,300 --> 00:14:15,633
But, Joey, you still put
yourself in danger,

212
00:14:15,767 --> 00:14:17,300
along with this operation.

213
00:14:18,367 --> 00:14:19,733
Will I be charged?

214
00:14:20,600 --> 00:14:22,200
Let's just make sure
it doesn't happen again.

215
00:14:22,333 --> 00:14:24,033
It really shouldn't anymore.

216
00:14:30,100 --> 00:14:31,333
Excuse me.

217
00:14:32,367 --> 00:14:35,400
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

218
00:14:39,600 --> 00:14:41,200
What were you thinking, Joey?

219
00:14:41,867 --> 00:14:44,633
You put yourself in the middle
of the firefight again.

220
00:14:44,767 --> 00:14:46,767
- That's...
- Stupid?

221
00:14:47,367 --> 00:14:48,533
Then why don't you finish
saying it?

222
00:14:50,233 --> 00:14:52,000
If I do it, it's stupid?

223
00:14:52,267 --> 00:14:53,667
So, what about the things
you're telling my father?

224
00:14:53,800 --> 00:14:55,267
That I'm resourceful
and good at fighting...

225
00:14:55,400 --> 00:14:56,533
Was that all just a joke?

226
00:14:56,667 --> 00:14:59,533
What I'm saying is you keep
throwing yourself

227
00:14:59,667 --> 00:15:00,767
into danger recklessly.

228
00:15:00,900 --> 00:15:02,233
That's my choice.

229
00:15:02,533 --> 00:15:04,533
A choice you don't need
to understand.

230
00:15:04,667 --> 00:15:06,333
And it's my choice
not to abandon you.

231
00:15:06,467 --> 00:15:08,333
Why do you have to do that?

232
00:15:09,567 --> 00:15:13,033
I made a deal with you
to find Berdugo together.

233
00:15:13,300 --> 00:15:14,600
But nowhere in that deal
did it say

234
00:15:14,733 --> 00:15:16,567
that my life depends on you.

235
00:15:16,700 --> 00:15:19,533
I don't want you
always worrying about me.

236
00:15:19,667 --> 00:15:21,900
I don't want you
always saving me.

237
00:15:22,200 --> 00:15:23,933
What's so wrong with that?

238
00:15:24,167 --> 00:15:26,367
That's why I'm with you,
isn't it?

239
00:15:26,500 --> 00:15:28,633
But you won't always be there.

240
00:15:29,900 --> 00:15:31,600
That's why I don't want
to get used to it.

241
00:15:31,733 --> 00:15:34,833
Why don't you just let me be?
Let me learn.

242
00:15:35,333 --> 00:15:37,500
Let me get hurt
and fight on my own.

243
00:15:37,633 --> 00:15:40,133
Joey, I can't just watch
silently

244
00:15:40,267 --> 00:15:43,067
while you put yourself
in danger.

245
00:15:48,033 --> 00:15:50,133
[ZOEY CLEARS THROAT]

246
00:15:51,533 --> 00:15:55,467
I hope I'm not interrupting,
but I have something to say.

247
00:15:55,600 --> 00:15:58,600
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

248
00:16:05,033 --> 00:16:10,767
Birthdays, anniversaries,
even simple dinners.

249
00:16:10,933 --> 00:16:13,033
He wants us to have photos

250
00:16:13,167 --> 00:16:15,400
because he says
he wants to capture

251
00:16:15,533 --> 00:16:18,200
how happy we are
in those moments.

252
00:16:18,533 --> 00:16:20,967
Sir Tomas is really sweet.

253
00:16:22,567 --> 00:16:25,967
But, Ma'am, Sir Tomas...

254
00:16:27,033 --> 00:16:29,733
he seems like a very private
person, doesn't he?

255
00:16:29,867 --> 00:16:30,933
Extremely.

256
00:16:31,067 --> 00:16:34,800
Even I don't know everything
he does.

257
00:16:34,933 --> 00:16:38,100
He says that
if I love him enough,

258
00:16:38,233 --> 00:16:44,267
then I should trust him in the
things I don't need to know.

259
00:16:44,433 --> 00:16:46,400
- [CHUCKLES SOFTLY]
- [PHONE RINGING]

260
00:16:47,700 --> 00:16:48,700
Wait.

261
00:16:50,233 --> 00:16:51,700
Hello, Hon?

262
00:16:53,333 --> 00:16:54,533
Okay.

263
00:16:54,667 --> 00:16:56,033
That's good.

264
00:16:56,167 --> 00:16:57,833
Okay, I'll see you.

265
00:16:59,567 --> 00:17:00,667
Hey.

266
00:17:01,700 --> 00:17:03,000
Tomas is coming home,

267
00:17:03,133 --> 00:17:06,900
so I'll talk to nanny to cook,
all right?

268
00:17:07,033 --> 00:17:08,667
- All right.
- See you.

269
00:17:21,633 --> 00:17:23,967
A person who is too private...

270
00:17:25,267 --> 00:17:27,867
often has many things to hide.

271
00:17:29,567 --> 00:17:36,467
So, you heard us, Ma'am.

272
00:17:40,233 --> 00:17:41,467
But...

273
00:17:42,800 --> 00:17:50,200
Ma'am, I'm sorry.
I don't mean to meddle, but...

274
00:17:50,367 --> 00:17:53,833
why don't you tell Ma'am Yvette

275
00:17:53,967 --> 00:17:57,233
if you have a problem
with Sir Tomas?

276
00:18:01,200 --> 00:18:03,500
She wouldn't want to know.

277
00:18:03,633 --> 00:18:05,633
But why?

278
00:18:05,767 --> 00:18:08,467
Why don't you like Sir Tomas?

279
00:18:09,500 --> 00:18:11,400
<i> This ends today, Tomas.</i>

280
00:18:11,533 --> 00:18:15,300
<i>My credibility took decades
to build,</i>

281
00:18:15,433 --> 00:18:18,467
<i>and I refuse to let it rot
like this.</i>

282
00:18:19,500 --> 00:18:21,833
<i> [INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]</i>

283
00:18:22,000 --> 00:18:24,633
<i>Does it pay better
than practicality?</i>

284
00:18:24,767 --> 00:18:27,967
<i> Yes, of course.</i>

285
00:18:28,100 --> 00:18:30,567
<i> Things money can't buy...</i>

286
00:18:30,700 --> 00:18:34,900
<i>peace of mind, a quiet life,
and most importantly,</i>

287
00:18:35,033 --> 00:18:37,167
<i> the safety of family.</i>

288
00:18:37,300 --> 00:18:40,567
<i>Then let me just remind you,
Rebecca.</i>

289
00:18:40,700 --> 00:18:47,500
<i>It wasn't this network that
gave you safety and comfort.</i>

290
00:18:49,233 --> 00:18:51,167
<i> It was me, Rebecca.</i>

291
00:18:51,300 --> 00:18:53,367
<i> I did my part.</i>

292
00:18:53,500 --> 00:18:58,033
<i>I buried the truths
you wanted hidden.</i>

293
00:18:59,433 --> 00:19:02,367
<i>And I'm done risking
my children's lives</i>

294
00:19:02,500 --> 00:19:04,600
<i> for your operations.</i>

295
00:19:04,733 --> 00:19:08,200
<i>You can't just walk away from
something like this, Rebecca.</i>

296
00:19:08,333 --> 00:19:10,600
<i>Not when you've been
in the circle too long.</i>

297
00:19:10,733 --> 00:19:12,633
<i> You know too much.</i>

298
00:19:12,767 --> 00:19:13,900
<i> Well...</i>

299
00:19:14,933 --> 00:19:16,233
<i> watch me.</i>

300
00:19:18,800 --> 00:19:21,767
<i> And if I don't let you go?</i>

301
00:19:21,900 --> 00:19:23,633
<i> Then...</i>

302
00:19:23,767 --> 00:19:27,033
<i> I'll tell Yvette everything.</i>

303
00:19:27,167 --> 00:19:31,700
<i> Every lie, every drug deal.</i>

304
00:19:31,867 --> 00:19:33,433
<i> Be careful, Rebecca.</i>

305
00:19:34,700 --> 00:19:37,967
<i>Some truths are dangerous
to the one who delivers them.</i>

306
00:19:38,100 --> 00:19:40,067
<i> Are you threatening me?</i>

307
00:19:40,200 --> 00:19:42,367
<i> All I'm saying is, Rebecca...</i>

308
00:19:42,500 --> 00:19:45,733
<i> this world is dangerous.</i>

309
00:19:47,000 --> 00:19:48,167
<i> [GASPING]</i>

310
00:19:49,233 --> 00:19:50,200
<i> [CROWD CLAMORING]</i>

311
00:19:51,267 --> 00:19:52,633
<i> And unfair.</i>

312
00:19:52,767 --> 00:19:54,400
<i>- Andrew!
- [GUN FIRES]</i>

313
00:19:56,733 --> 00:19:58,600
<i> You've made enemies.</i>

314
00:20:00,567 --> 00:20:03,533
<i>And if something
were to happen to you,</i>

315
00:20:03,700 --> 00:20:06,000
<i> they wouldn't be surprised.</i>

316
00:20:06,133 --> 00:20:08,667
<i> So be careful out there.</i>

317
00:20:09,967 --> 00:20:12,000
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

318
00:20:12,133 --> 00:20:13,367
<i> For me.</i>

319
00:20:16,500 --> 00:20:17,933
<i> For Yvette.</i>

320
00:20:21,000 --> 00:20:23,033
<i> And for your grandchildren.</i>

321
00:20:25,767 --> 00:20:27,933
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

322
00:20:33,400 --> 00:20:35,033
Ma'am Rebecca...

323
00:20:36,767 --> 00:20:38,300
are you okay?

324
00:20:39,967 --> 00:20:41,700
Just remember...

325
00:20:41,833 --> 00:20:46,100
do not trust Tomas.

326
00:20:48,633 --> 00:20:51,667
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

327
00:21:00,333 --> 00:21:02,967
Joey, you've been there
all along?

328
00:21:03,100 --> 00:21:04,367
A little while, yes.

329
00:21:06,767 --> 00:21:08,100
So...

330
00:21:08,267 --> 00:21:12,133
do you have any news
from the precinct?

331
00:21:14,033 --> 00:21:15,900
I'm sick and tired
of their excuses

332
00:21:16,033 --> 00:21:19,567
about your father's body.

333
00:21:19,700 --> 00:21:22,400
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

334
00:21:22,533 --> 00:21:23,533
My dear...

335
00:21:25,567 --> 00:21:27,300
My dear, is there a problem?

336
00:21:28,633 --> 00:21:33,633
Remember, I told you
to tell me everything,

337
00:21:34,833 --> 00:21:37,900
especially if you're going
through something difficult.

338
00:21:39,433 --> 00:21:45,200
It's just the two of us now,
so I want us to be okay.

339
00:21:45,367 --> 00:21:46,967
What's wrong?

340
00:21:48,000 --> 00:21:49,367
Nothing, Mom.

341
00:21:52,533 --> 00:21:56,567
I just wanted to tell you
something.

342
00:21:56,700 --> 00:21:58,200
[GATE CREAKING]

343
00:21:58,333 --> 00:22:00,300
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

344
00:22:24,367 --> 00:22:30,833
[UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING]

345
00:22:30,967 --> 00:22:32,733
The case I'm handling now

346
00:22:32,867 --> 00:22:35,467
is the biggest drug syndicate
in the Philippines.

347
00:22:35,600 --> 00:22:36,800
Berdugo is real.

348
00:22:36,933 --> 00:22:40,333
What's more important?
Andrew or your business?

349
00:22:40,467 --> 00:22:42,500
Nothing matters more to me

350
00:22:42,633 --> 00:22:46,500
than my family and the business
that keeps us alive.

351
00:22:46,633 --> 00:22:47,833
I found this.

352
00:22:47,967 --> 00:22:48,867
There's an engraving.

353
00:22:49,033 --> 00:22:50,367
I need to finish the mission.

354
00:22:50,500 --> 00:22:53,867
I promise, after this mission,
Berdugo will be behind bars.

355
00:22:54,000 --> 00:22:55,267
Was the deal finalized?

356
00:22:55,400 --> 00:22:57,233
Unfortunately, not.

357
00:22:57,367 --> 00:22:58,667
Tomas, is that blood?

358
00:22:58,800 --> 00:23:00,133
Why, Hon?
Where did you get hurt?

359
00:23:00,267 --> 00:23:02,167
I got this.
I'll just change the bandage.

360
00:23:02,300 --> 00:23:03,833
Yvette, it's not just
a small cut.

361
00:23:03,967 --> 00:23:05,200
What do you mean?

362
00:23:06,567 --> 00:23:10,033
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]
